# Fluree Memory — repo-scoped
# Auto-managed by `fluree memory`. Manual edits are supported.
@prefix mem: <https://ns.flur.ee/memory#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

mem:constraint-01m5x1zt7w483hs4ddjdqtbd77 a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "serve must never thread/resume a Codex thread whose join wasn't classified codexHost daemon (loaded in this machine's daemon at bus_join). Other threads get messages only while the daemon has them loaded; an active-writer refusal means wait, not retry; subagents are never woken." ;
    mem:tag "app-server" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "guard" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/mcp.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.044903+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "A thread has one writer. Resuming a desktop-app thread once the app released it made the daemon its writer and locked the owner's window ('open in another app'). Classifying at join works because a Codex agent calls bus_join mid-turn, while its thread is loaded wherever it runs." ;
    mem:alternatives "a per-session wake flag (records permission, doesn't reconcile two writers),retrying with back-off until the thread is free" .

mem:constraint-01m5x1ztaxvc47hyxyyrwbtsrb a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "The Codex Stop hook must deliver only when transcript_path names the thread in session_id (rollout files are named by thread id): a subagent's hook carries its parent's session_id and would otherwise take the parent's messages. Any failure must let the turn end." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "subagents" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/hook.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.141430+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Codex documents that subagent hooks use the parent session id; a hook that errors or blocks would stall the user's thread." .

mem:constraint-01m5x9h52psxmgtkmg6pxw27q8 a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "A process started from a session's shell inherits that session's runtime id (codex exec from Claude inherits CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), so the CLI acts as the parent when it defaults --runtime to the address's runtime. Give delegates that need an inbox their own address." ;
    mem:tag "delegates" ;
    mem:tag "identity" ;
    mem:tag "ownership" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "should" ;
    mem:artifactRef "README.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T23:43:02.230648+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:constraint-01m5xn3cfyazcft2fzpm61vfvp a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "thread/queue/add does not deduplicate on clientUserMessageId: adding twice queues two items, and the desktop runs both. List the thread's queue before adding. The thread/queue/* methods are experimental (initialize with experimentalApi); use the desktop's bundled CLI so they match the app that runs the items." ;
    mem:tag "app-server" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:05:13.982763+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:decision-01m5x1zt1sy4dfmyp66p7ah4ep a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Each machine runs one agent-bus serve that owns the store for that machine's sessions; sessions and the CLI reach it over MCP (streamable HTTP on loopback), and it also runs the Codex deliverer." ;
    mem:tag "architecture" ;
    mem:tag "mcp" ;
    mem:tag "serve" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/serve.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:13.849993+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "One process gives one cursor writer per address, one per-address lock (Bus.deliver) shared by reads and deliveries, and one ledger change stream; only serve holds the Fluree token." ;
    mem:alternatives "a stdio MCP server per session (raced on cursors and needed the token in every session),Fluree's native MCP endpoint for agents,a separate deliver-codex process" .

mem:decision-01m5x1zt365xpe32kp3h35dkww a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Messages live in a Fluree ledger (one message per insert commit, a cursor is the last commit t read), behind the Ledger service, with a JSONL file as the fallback store." ;
    mem:tag "fluree" ;
    mem:tag "ledger" ;
    mem:tag "storage" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Fluree.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Ledger.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:13.894070+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The ledger is queryable (SPARQL SELECT and full-text through bus_query and bus_history), readable as of any t, and shared by every machine through one transaction server; the JSONL store keeps the bus usable without Fluree." ;
    mem:alternatives "JSONL only,SQLite" .

mem:decision-01m5x1zt4q2fm8vdq3ezve2sw5 a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Messages record their origin (machine, the sender's joined cwd, its repo and branch) and are grouped into commit windows by repo and ts against that repo's commit times; no message stores a Git SHA." ;
    mem:tag "commit-windows" ;
    mem:tag "git" ;
    mem:tag "origin" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/domain.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:13.943795+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "A SHA per message costs a git call on every send and says nothing for uncommitted work; commit times already order messages against the code they discuss." ;
    mem:alternatives "a Git SHA per message" .

mem:decision-01m5x1zt6aegrjnxxakxym735x a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Codex threads are woken by push: serve sends the unread messages as turn/start through the machine's Codex app-server daemon, which starts a turn on an idle thread and steers a running one. Messages are marked read only once the daemon accepts." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "delivery" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:13.994666+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Agents are woken, never polled; a Codex agent can't run a background wait the way Claude Code can." ;
    mem:alternatives "agents polling with bus_wait,a queued-input command" .

mem:decision-01m5x1zt9exbx6s973sqkt00kh a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Codex desktop Local threads stay in the desktop app's own app-server. The bus wakes them, idle or busy, with a nudge in their own queue (see the queue-wake decision); the Codex Stop hook (agent-bus codex-stop-hook) also continues an ending turn with the thread's unread messages, and is optional since the nudge shipped." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "desktop" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/connections.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/hook.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.094317+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T03:05:13.937520+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Moving desktop threads onto the daemon loses desktop features the owner needs: SSH projects lose browser and computer use, automations and the artifact viewer, and probably Handoff and the thread tools; the CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_URL override skips the app's provisioning too." ;
    mem:alternatives "a desktop SSH project to the same machine,launching the app with CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_URL,deep links (they only prefill the composer)" .

mem:decision-01m5x9h50yh252vteyr31k9jtk a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Each bus address is owned by one session, identified by (runtime, the runtime's own id: CODEX_THREAD_ID or CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), passed as an explicit session argument on every call and recorded in the presence entry. Only the owner reads, waits, leaves or sends from it; takeover must name the holder's join id." ;
    mem:tag "addresses" ;
    mem:tag "identity" ;
    mem:tag "ownership" ;
    mem:tag "takeover" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/address-ownership.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/client.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T23:43:02.174817+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Two sessions on one address were competing consumers: a reply went to the wrong session. Runtime ids survive compaction and reach background waits and hooks without extra storage." ;
    mem:alternatives "lease token issued at join (must survive compaction and be handed to waits and hooks),identity in an HTTP header (connection headers stay fixed across /clear; one Codex daemon serves many threads),idle-based automatic takeover (inactivity cannot prove a session ended)" .

mem:decision-01m5xn3ccvw8spz95s87csea3r a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Codex threads not on the daemon (desktop Local threads, or a daemon join whose resume another app-server refused) are woken by a nudge in their own queue: serve starts a short-lived app-server of its own on stdio (the desktop's bundled CLI, serve --codex), lists the thread's queue (thread/queue/list) and adds one fixed nudge (thread/queue/add) only when none of ours waits for that address. The nudge carries no text from other sessions and marks nothing read; the thread's own bus_read moves its cursor. Shipped in 3d10fca, qualified live 2026-10-27." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "delivery" ;
    mem:tag "desktop" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/queue-wake.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:05:13.883838+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The desktop app runs a queued item as a turn within seconds in an idle open thread and stays the thread's only writer. Listing before adding keeps at most one nudge waiting, which bounds empty turns to one per read, survives serve restarts and reconciles adds whose outcome is unknown." ;
    mem:alternatives "the desktop coordination socket (spike, never run past Gate 0),a heartbeat automation in the thread (crude fallback only),the daemon taking the thread (second writer locks the owner out),the codex queue CLI with an in-memory mark (reads before a nudge runs stack empty turns; timed-out adds force duplicate or missed wake),thread/queue/start (could run the item in an app-server that is not the thread's owner)" .

mem:fact-01m5x1ztcfrgxg1r3zcbxt5s0f a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The bus's Fluree token has no subject and is sent only to the data and admin APIs; the event stream stays open. In Fluree 4.2.4 a token with a subject is held to identity policies, which deny writes on a ledger without policies, and events auth refuses subject-less tokens. With CORS off, a cross-origin text/plain POST still writes, so auth is what protects the loopback server." ;
    mem:tag "auth" ;
    mem:tag "fluree" ;
    mem:tag "security" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "scripts/install-launch-agents.sh" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Fluree.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.191984+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Each of these was found by a failing write or test during setup." .

mem:fact-01m5x1zte4rznzfcj9npy234jz a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "HttpRouter.serve forks its layer memo map, so a service built inside it is a separate instance from one built outside. Provide Bus (and the Ledger) around Serve.layer, never inside the router, or the MCP tools and the Codex deliverer get separate cursors and locks." ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "layers" ;
    mem:tag "serve" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/serve.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.244634+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Found in Effect 4.0.6's source while wiring serve; nothing fails visibly, deliveries just stop being serialized with reads." .

mem:fact-01m5x1ztfs8vfda4m06w25nvj8 a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "codex app-server daemon restart and stop refuse a daemon the CLI auto-started on first use ('not managed by codex app-server daemon'), and a running daemon never updates itself. To replace one: kill -TERM it, then run codex app-server daemon start from a shell with ulimit -S -n 10240. Restarting drops its loaded threads." ;
    mem:tag "app-server" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "daemon" ;
    mem:tag "operations" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "README.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.297018+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The daemon inherits its starter's open-file limit (macOS default 256), and each loaded thread costs about 33 descriptors, so a few threads exhaust it." .

mem:fact-01m5xn3chn8n8q5wktct3xxn4s a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "A Codex thread has no rollout until its first turn, so thread/queue/add for a just-started thread fails with 'no rollout found'; that error can be temporary and is retried. Separately, codex exec reads stdin when it is not a terminal and waits on it, even with a prompt argument: run it with < /dev/null in scripts." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "exec" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "rollout" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/queue-wake.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:05:14.037431+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
